#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203687 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203921 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80cffe94-4f90-5bd8-b0b3-c09d54100580" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations"}] :question/id #uuid "058f91e1-7365-5ee5-8c35-0eaa433db282" :question/math-academy-id "e-14616" :question/problem "Consider the following relation defined on the set $A = \\{-2,0,2 \\}$.\n\n$R = \\big\\{(-2,-2), (-2,0), (0,0), (2,-2), (2,0) \\big\\}$\n\nDetermine whether the relation is reflexive, irreflexive, or neither." :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R$, defined on a set $A$, is\n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x) \\in R$ for all $x \\in A$,\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x) \\notin R$ for all $x \\in A$.\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nIn our case, the relation is defined on $\\{-2,0,2 \\}$, and we have\n\n$$\n(-2,-2) \\in R, \\qquad (0,0) \\in R, \\qquad (2,2) \\notin R\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can conclude the following:\n\n$\\qquad$ Since $(2,2) \\notin R$ and $(0,0) \\in R$, the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203688 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203922 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4b47a31-7bda-5366-bac4-1d070776e776" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations From a Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "5a1a0f7a-d39c-5551-a512-5fd1bea5b3cb" :question/math-academy-id "e-14620" :question/problem "![](images/a5/a5d6068e6098da0c8164a2afe50c6b6e184366a1ecec96d4032eb35928b67285.png)\n\nWhich digraphs represent a relation, defined on the set $A = \\{\\spadesuit, \\heartsuit, \\clubsuit\\}$, that is neither reflexive nor irreflexive?" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R$, defined on a set $A$, is\n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x) \\in R$ for all $x \\in A$,\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x) \\notin R$ for all $x \\in A$.\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nPairs of the form $(x,x)$ correspond to the loops that start and finish at the same node in the directed graphs.\n\nSince $R$ must be neither reflexive nor irreflexive, we require that some nodes (vertices) have a loop and some don't. Among the given options, only digraph III has this property:\n\n![](images/a8/a834e4d6937327c01094409529596d36ac292c590d9ec9defe9d2fbac0bef983.png)\n\nNotice that the nodes $\\spadesuit$ and $\\heartsuit$ have loops, while the node $\\clubsuit$ does not have a loop."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203689 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "306be17f-f950-57e2-9cb7-2b33c8a4929e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations Over Infinite Sets"}] :question/id #uuid "76419f6e-45a2-5af2-b048-2f7c323db796" :question/math-academy-id "e-14621" :question/problem "Which of the following relations are reflexive?\n\n- $x \\: R \\: y$ if and only if $2 \\mid (y+x)$, defined on $\\mathbb{Z}$\n- $x \\: S \\: y$ if and only if $x \\not\\mid y$, defined on $\\mathbb{Z}$\n- $x \\: T \\: y$ if and only if $3 \\mid (x^2+y)$, defined on $\\mathbb{Z}$" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R$, defined on a set $A$, is\n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x) \\in R$ for all $x \\in A$,\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x) \\notin R$ for all $x \\in A$.\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our relations.\n\n- Relation $R$ is reflexive. Indeed, $(x,x) \\in R$ for all $x \\in \\mathbb{Z}$. Notice that\n$2\\mid (x+x)$\nfor any $x \\in \\mathbb{Z}$.\n- Relation $S$ is irreflexive. Indeed, $(x,x) \\notin S$ for all $x \\in \\mathbb{Z}$. Notice that\n$x \\mid x$\nfor any $x \\in \\mathbb{Z}$.\n- Relation $T$ is neither reflexive nor irreflexive. Notice that $(1,1) \\notin T$ since $3 \\not \\mid (1^2+1)$, while $(0,0) \\in T$ since $3 \\mid (0^2+0)$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$R$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204235 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203922 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4b47a31-7bda-5366-bac4-1d070776e776" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8925b00a-fade-5f5f-ab17-e0c1e6c13338" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/90/903c7d67b71386355439cb39a724c6be874ba4c7e3026343d91b429e649fac81.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200081} {:answer/id #uuid "c70241ba-4710-5e7b-97ab-819d65347db1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/84/847bcee3b9f9fc6672d5858111866141e043e390605cd92fb5579fd5193d7df4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200082} {:answer/id #uuid "f81f69d9-4c7f-5b42-ae1c-4c808a5c8afb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/95/95d0b20c7f11f2242c5e22ed8d66721cd8f0076ea5f0c8f0a996d8536fbd2a35.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200083} {:answer/id #uuid "6af3321c-cbc7-579e-8b49-c50c5dcc2954" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/dd/ddfa6dfdf196e05ed653672d0e7c4369c75674e885d98b89abf1fdf0e4425474.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200084} {:answer/id #uuid "7fa97445-deaa-5077-8244-971f7543b207" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cf/cf92336ff9f0a22f7ab5f30e3f3b336dab6f884b72a8deeccfdb00c3f926c5a7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200085}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f38f6dcc-8503-580d-bb03-02474c761e75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200080}] :question/id #uuid "d46c6540-3ee2-574b-ab89-04b06559d4b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-212207" :question/problem "Which of the following digraphs represent a relation, defined on the set $A = {1, 2, 3}$, that is neither reflexive nor irreflexive?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204236 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "306be17f-f950-57e2-9cb7-2b33c8a4929e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations Over Infinite Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81d093bf-7907-5f7b-8280-06d76d61b530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "and $(-1,-1) ∈ R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200087} {:answer/id #uuid "8ad92361-efd5-5440-9d3b-63ee65139347" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "for all $x ∈ A$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200088} {:answer/id #uuid "8deb48ca-d434-5b1a-a6f2-27306deeb446" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "and $(0, 0) ∈ R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200089}] :answer-field/id #uuid "586522fd-5861-55b7-81e7-43499c023668" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200086} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "891c7c6b-70e2-5d83-b66c-b318f83a1f79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, x) ∉ R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200091} {:answer/id #uuid "c0db131f-b40a-5c88-9273-27891c87a60a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-1) ∉ R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200092} {:answer/id #uuid "d661a8e0-3e42-5d76-8c1d-b49228242d6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, x) ∈ R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200093} {:answer/id #uuid "4e312260-bf36-5981-ba3d-a747cbc02dcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0, 0) ∉ R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200094}] :answer-field/id #uuid "accd1960-0427-5e3d-ad02-e06f3da30981" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200090} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9255ac6d-8d77-52cb-be1f-d6f29ac8ced3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "irreflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200096} {:answer/id #uuid "9f874a65-bc51-5b41-ac9f-af8ee314bcf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "both reflexive and irreflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200097} {:answer/id #uuid "35e4bec4-f63b-50d8-8633-427d25cd3f71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "reflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200098} {:answer/id #uuid "7ea8fa54-cd57-5daa-8a06-857b33eb4a19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "neither reflexive nor irreflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200099}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f5b5fb67-cda7-57bd-abcb-0c416cd0ef2a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186200095}] :question/id #uuid "a78cb3d5-72f7-5878-912d-51497cf297ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-212208" :question/problem "Let $R$ be a relation defined on the set $Z$ as follows:\n\n$xRy$ if and only if $x - y^{2} = 0$\n\nSelect the options that make the following reasoning correct:\n\nSince\n{{field-1}} {{field-2}},\n\nthe relation is\n{{field-3}}."}]}
